Scale Up
========

Overview
--------
This builds on the secured and monitored setup by scaling up to 4
servers total: 2 load balancers (set up as a cluster), plus 2 servers
where each piece (web server, app server, database) now gets its own
dedicated server instead of sharing one.

What got added, and why
-------------------------
- 1 more load balancer (HAProxy), clustered with the first one:
  gets rid of the load balancer as a weak point. If one goes down,
  the other takes over, since they're set up together as a cluster
  (active-active or active-passive) sharing a virtual IP.
- 1 more server, splitting the web server, app server, and database
  onto their own dedicated machines: each piece now gets its own
  CPU, memory, and disk. So if one (say, the database) gets hit hard,
  it doesn't drag down the others. It also means you can scale each
  layer on its own, based on what it actually needs.

Quick summary of why each piece was added
--------------------------------------
- 2nd load balancer: removes the load balancer as a weak point, keeps
  the entry point to the site always available.
- Dedicated web server machine: can be tuned/scaled just for handling
  HTTP requests and static files.
- Dedicated app server machine: can be tuned/scaled just for running
  the app's logic, without the web server's load affecting it.
- Dedicated database machine: can be tuned/scaled just for storing
  and retrieving data, separate from the web/app load.
